  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThe cooling trend will continue through the week with highs in the \n90s across much of the region everyday. Thursday looks to be the \ncoolest day this week with highs in the lower 90s across the far \nsouthwestern Texas Panhandle and upper 90s across the southern \nRolling Plains. Chances for thunderstorms return again Wednesday and \nThursday. A very similar set up as expected Tuesday evening is \nexpected Wednesday afternoon and evening. Upslope flow will result \nin isolated to scattered thunderstorms developing over higher \nterrain in NM and CO. Northwesterly flow will push these storms \nsoutheast into our CWA. By the weekend, an upper trough will swing \nacross the Pacific Northwest, causing the upper ridging to expand \nback to the east across our region. This will dry out conditions and \nwarm temperatures back into the triple digits.",
